{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the R diagnosis 2dfa33b8: the maintained Lending case\nmoves to the base family. Rules 6 stays as it is.\n\nReason. Rules 6 admits no capability, and that refusal is correct.\nEvery new room is founded in the base family, and `lending-library`\nis a base room. The current Lending package declares\n`publication-paths@1`, so the base family is the only family that\ninstalls it. The test must follow the path a member takes.\n\n1. In `maintained-application-projections.test.ts`, each row names\n   its cohort. The Counter row keeps `DECLARED_APPLICATION_COHORT`.\n   The Lending row founds `BASE_COHORT`. The test title prints the\n   cohort. Keep every assertion of both rows.\n2. Add one Plain case to\n   `packages/platform/test/application-install-v2.test.ts`: the\n   declared rules refuse a package that declares a capability, with\n   `invalid-application-package`. The same package without the\n   capability is the control. This case keeps the old cohort's limit\n   as a stated fact.\n3. The change stays in tests and test fixtures. If the Lending row\n   needs a production change on the base family, stop and send the\n   fact. A missing browser read on the base family is a finding for\n   R, not a reason to narrow the row.\n4. Your limits stand: keep the capability, keep Rules 6, keep the\n   assertions, and claim no old-cohort proof from the base run.\n\nOrder. E1 keeps the slot. R integrates the main that holds E1, then\nrepeats the identifier comparison, because both heads change\nLending. Before the R gate START, run three owners alone and state\neach result: `application-examples.test.ts`, the new Plain case and\nthe maintained projection file in Native. Then run one gate. The\ncombined route of da772676 holds for R with LP-1.\n\nSeen: the E1 comparison END abc8e07e. Grow 2.0.0 is exact, and only\nthe two presentation identifiers change. Apply them and continue to\nthe E1 gate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699